{
  "_about": [
    "Golden question set for retrieval evaluation.",
    "",
    "Written against the synthetic demo corpus in backend/fixtures/demo/. The",
    "candidate (Alex Moran) is a backend engineer with Go, Python, PostgreSQL and",
    "Kafka; Northwind is a strong fit, Vertex is partial (no Kubernetes, no",
    "Terraform), Helio is weak (ML platform, a different domain).",
    "",
    "`must_retrieve` uses tags from evals/tagger.py (<document>:<section>), not",
    "chunk ids, so the set survives re-chunking.",
    "",
    "REVIEWER NOTE: these questions were drafted alongside the implementation.",
    "docs/PLAN.md is explicit that a golden set authored by the same process that",
    "built the retriever is weak evidence \u2014 it measures regression, not quality,",
    "and it is not adversarial. Treat the numbers as a regression gate. Replacing",
    "these with independently written questions is the single highest-value",
    "improvement available to this eval.",
    "",
    "`expected_missing` lists must-have requirements the candidate genuinely lacks, judged against the r\u00e9sum\u00e9 by hand. Scoped to must-haves so a nice-to-have the candidate happens to lack is not counted as a gap."
  ],
